"""Casual and optimized party presets, generated by explicit rules.

"standard" is the existing builds (fighter_5, ...). This module writes
{class}_{level}_{profile}.yaml for the casual and optimized profiles at levels
1, 3, 5, 7 and 10, using only what the builder supports. Feats other than
ASIs, species and multiclassing are out of the builder's scope, so
"optimized" is a careful single-class character rather than a full min-maxer.

    python -m engine.presets --write

Casual: a reasonable player who builds for flavour. Standard array with the
primary ability at 14 and a flavour ability at 15, a +1/+1/+1 background,
ASIs split between primary and flavour, sword-and-board or utility picks,
thematic spells, and no reaction spells (Shield, Counterspell).

Optimized: conventional optimization within scope. Point buy 15/15/14 into
primary, Constitution and the most useful third ability, a +2 primary / +1
Constitution background, ASIs into the primary until 20 and then
Constitution, the strongest equipment and style, and spells chosen for
combat value first.
"""
